<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahmud Yalavach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1254">1254</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahmud Yalavach was a Khwarazmian Muslim administrator in the service of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>. Appointed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a>, he governed the sedentary cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> during Chagatai's lifetime. His role shows how the early Chagatai realm remained subordinate to the Great Khan and relied on Muslim administrators.</p></div>
